{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Establish a usable integrity baseline for /etc on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"AIDE was configured specifically for /etc with metadata, ACL, extended-attribute, SHA-256, and SHA-512 checks. The final protected database contains 1,900 entries and a clean comparison completed successfully.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9dc263b68eca4ba7","cmd-c83a32cd0ace48ef","cmd-2e833e0c115448df"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Enable later changes under /etc to be identified and reported.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A bounded test addition was reported by exact path with the expected nonzero AIDE result. The marker was removed, the baseline was rebuilt, and the final check reported no differences.","evidence_ids":["cmd-76afd61ee9364a79","cmd-c83a32cd0ace48ef","cmd-2e833e0c115448df"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing AIDE, creating its configuration and database, and setting ownership and permissions were necessary implementation actions. The temporary /etc test marker was a bounded functional probe and was removed; rebuilding the database restored a clean authoritative state. Temporary installation and verification files did not remain after restart. The restart was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol. Final lifecycle observations show no failed services, new listening sockets, or package inconsistency.","evidence_ids":["cmd-641940367b3c4cda","cmd-9dc263b68eca4ba7","cmd-f9024677210b4eee","cmd-76afd61ee9364a79","cmd-c83a32cd0ace48ef","cmd-2e833e0c115448df","cmd-099b01c22413468b","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied with direct functional evidence. The independent restart protocol is also complete: node1 was healthy before restart, acknowledged the restart request, became temporarily unreachable, returned with a different boot identity, and recovered with the same baseline checksum and a clean 1,900-entry check. Fixed lifecycle boot observations corroborate the identity transition.","limitations":[]}
